  <name>Organic Maps (GTK)</name>
  <summary>Offline maps and navigation</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.x_vlad_x">
    <name>Vladislav Shadiuk</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      An unofficial native GNOME interface for the Organic Maps core, made for Linux phones
      and usable on desktops. Maps, search and routing work without an internet connection
      once the regions you need are downloaded.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Full-screen GPU map with touch gestures: drag, pinch, rotation, double tap</li>
      <li>Offline search with categories, history and results on the map</li>
      <li>Routing for car, walking, cycling and public transport, with turn-by-turn voice guidance</li>
      <li>Map downloader with region search and updates</li>
      <li>Bookmarks and tracks, KML, KMZ and GPX import, track recording</li>
      <li>Outdoor, hiking, cycling, isoline and subway layers; night mode</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This application is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Organic Maps project.
      Map data © OpenStreetMap contributors.
    </p>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.x_vlad_x.OrganicMapsGtk.desktop</launchable>

